    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0527" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg455"/>

                <head>No. 273.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Hamlin</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 195, of the 2d
                    November last, to Mr. Fairchild, and other correspondence, I inclose, as a
                    further paper connected with the subject of that instruction, a copy of a letter
                    from Mr. Houghton, secretary of the Maritime Association of New York, and of a
                    memorial of that association, respecting the charge of 10 cents per ton levied
                    by the Spanish consul there on cargoes for Cuba and Porto Rico.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FEED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d337-a1.xml" xpointer="d337-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d337-a2.xml" xpointer="d337-a2"/>
